---
const rows = [
  {
    lead: "You're here because you've felt what this work can do.",
    rest: "Maybe a single workshop already shifted something old. Maybe you've been with the 12-week course and you don't want to stop.",
  },
  {
    lead: 'You want to go deeper.',
    rest: 'Not just for one more healing experience, but to learn the work from the inside out.',
  },
  {
    lead: 'You want to hold space.',
    rest: 'Maybe for one person at a time, maybe for a group, maybe for yourself. You want to know how to do it well.',
  },
  {
    lead: "You're a practitioner already",
    rest: '— therapist, coach, sound healer, breathworker, psychologist, body worker, teacher — and you want a tool that reaches the layers your current tools cannot.',
  },
  {
    lead: 'Or you have no professional ambition at all,',
    rest: 'and you simply want this for yourself. That is enough.',
  },
];
---

<section class="cc-forwhom">
  <div class="cc-forwhom-bg" aria-hidden="true">
    <img
      src="/media/library/svh-retreat-sounding-blue.webp"
      alt=""
      loading="lazy"
    />
  </div>
  <div class="cc-forwhom-inner">
    <div class="cc-forwhom-head">
      <div class="cc-eyebrow cc-eyebrow--center">Who this is for</div>
      <h2 class="cc-h2" style="margin-top: var(--sp-4); max-width: 26ch; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
        For those who recognise <em>some of the following.</em>
      </h2>
    </div>

    <ul class="cc-forwhom-list">
      {rows.map((r) => (
        <li>
          <strong>{r.lead}</strong>
          {r.rest}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <p class="cc-forwhom-note">
      A note on what this course is not: it is not a comprehensive training
      to become a therapist, coach, or psychologist. It is a course in
      Somatic Vocal Healing specifically. If you intend to work with clients
      professionally, you should already have a background in holding space
      and navigating emotional processes.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
